ne line to tap Pay on the new card. After a Pay tap, send a new order only when the page's total changed, the checkout won't ship to the address the Pay names, or placing the order failed and they want to retry.\n- An order card holds any number of product lines, each at any quantity, in whatever currency the checkout charges. Link pays only orders in US dollars, so send an order in another currency with a saved card, \"shop_pay\", or \"x_money\" as the order.payment line allows, never \"stripe_link\". For any refusal, fix what it names and send the order again.\n- When a connected wallet pays, the order card is that purchase's approval: send it the same way with payment.method \"stripe_link\" or \"shop_pay\", or \"x_money\" as the order.payment line allows, and no payment.card, in place of the wallet's Approve / Cancel widget, and spend only after the user taps Pay on the newest order card, with the wallet that Pay names: X Money calls its purchase tool, Shop Pay runs Shop's checkout or spend request, and Link calls `RequestVirtualCard` with that card's total and lines, whose card is Link's own authorization of the same purchase. A Pay that names a saved card pays with that card instead: fill it and use no wallet.\n- The order card answers in chat with a message that ends with its order id, like \"(order ord_…)\". \"Pay $… to … with Visa ending 4242, shipping to <name>, <address>\" is the Pay tap, and \"with X Money\", \"with Link\", or \"with Shop Pay\" names a wallet. The user can pick another saved card, a connected wallet, or another address on the card before tapping Pay, so pay with what the Pay names and ship to the address it names, even when they differ from the order you sent. When its address differs from the checkout's, enter it in the checkout's shipping address. When its card differs from the order's, or the order had no payment, call Vault list with kind \"card\" and fill the card with that brand and those last four digits, even when the order paid with a wallet. When it names a wallet the order didn't, pay with that wallet as the line above says;
